# "From Specification to Live Screen"


## SCENE 1 — Open 

> "For our SDLC on Developer phase we use Hexaware AI-Framework. //We proven this tool for core insurance systems — policy, billing, claims — . // They need speed *and* governance. // Today, I'm going to show you exactly how we deliver both — from a single line of business requirement, all the way to a live screen in Guidewire PolicyCenter."

> "Here's the tension. // Our AI Framework can draft Gosu, PCF, and test code in minutes — not days. // That's the upside. // But without guardrails, that same speed can draft its way past naming standards, past policy rules, past the one thing that actually protects a carrier: a human checkpoint before code ships. // So the question isn't *'should we use AI to build on PolicyCenter.'* // It's *'how do we use it responsibly.'*"

**[Slide 3 — A Governed AI Delivery Pipeline] Video Recording starting here** 

> "Our answer is a governed AI delivery pipeline, built on three gates. // First, a Knowledge Gate — every AI answer is grounded in your own architecture, through the Guidewire Developer Assistant, not generic training data. // Second, from our Docs Directory a Policy Gate — your naming conventions, your bundle discipline, your PII rules, translated into automatic, checkable rules. // And third — the one that matters most — a Human Review Gate. // Nothing reaches a trusted branch without a qualified reviewer's sign-off. // AI accelerates. Governance protects. People decide."

